--------------------------
LTE Cell Scanner / Tracker
--------------------------

This is a collection of tools to locate and track LTE basestation cells using
very low performance RF front ends. For example, these tools work with RTL2832
based dongles (E4000, R820T, etc.) which have a noise figure of 20dB, only 8
bits in the A/D, and a crystal with a frequency error of about 100 ppm.

The 'CellSearch' program can be used to search for LTE carriers within a range
of frequencies.  Once an LTE frequency has been located, 'LTE-Tracker' can be
used to monitor and track, in realtime, any LTE cells on that frequency.

The main documentation in html format can be found on the web at:
  http://www.evrytania.com/lte-tools
And in the doc/index.html subdirectory of this distribution.

For questions, comments, or bug reports, contact James Peroulas
james@evrytania.com, or check the bugtracker on github:
  https://github.com/Evrytania/LTE-Cell-Scanner/issues

------
Quick build instructions:
------
  cd LTE-Cell-Scanner
  mkdir build
  cd build
  cmake ..
  make

------
Building on macOS (Apple Silicon) with HackRF / PlutoSDR:
------
This fork builds and runs on macOS on Apple Silicon and adds a SoapySDR
front-end so it can be used with HackRF and PlutoSDR (in addition to RTL-SDR).

1. Install the dependencies with Homebrew:

     brew install cmake itpp fftw boost libomp soapysdr soapyhackrf
     # RTL-SDR support is optional:
     brew install librtlsdr

   For PlutoSDR (ADALM-PLUTO) you additionally need libiio, libad9361 and
   SoapyPlutoSDR, which are not in Homebrew. Build them from source into the
   Homebrew prefix (no sudo needed on Apple Silicon):

     # libiio (use v0.25; note OSX_FRAMEWORK=OFF so it installs a plain dylib)
     git clone -b v0.25 https://github.com/analogdevicesinc/libiio
     cmake -S libiio -B libiio/build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/homebrew \
       -DOSX_FRAMEWORK=OFF -DCMAKE_INSTALL_NAME_DIR=/opt/homebrew/lib -DWITH_LOCAL_BACKEND=OFF -DWITH_TESTS=OFF \
       -DWITH_DOC=OFF -DWITH_IIOD=OFF -DHAVE_DNS_SD=OFF
     cmake --build libiio/build -j4 && cmake --install libiio/build

     # libad9361
     git clone https://github.com/analogdevicesinc/libad9361-iio
     cmake -S libad9361-iio -B libad9361-iio/build \
       -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/homebrew -DOSX_FRAMEWORK=OFF -DCMAKE_INSTALL_NAME_DIR=/opt/homebrew/lib
     cmake --build libad9361-iio/build -j4 && cmake --install libad9361-iio/build

     # SoapyPlutoSDR (CMAKE_FIND_FRAMEWORK=NEVER avoids a stale /Library/Frameworks copy)
     git clone https://github.com/pothosware/SoapyPlutoSDR
     cmake -S SoapyPlutoSDR -B SoapyPlutoSDR/build \
       -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/homebrew -DCMAKE_FIND_FRAMEWORK=NEVER \
       -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/opt/homebrew
     cmake --build SoapyPlutoSDR/build -j4 && cmake --install SoapyPlutoSDR/build

   Verify both SDRs are visible:
     SoapySDRUtil --find     # lists hackrf and/or plutosdr
   (PlutoSDR tunes 325 MHz - 3.8 GHz, so use it only within that range.)

2. Build:

     cd LTE-Cell-Scanner
     mkdir build && cd build
     cmake ..
     make -j4

3. Verify the SDR is detected:

     SoapySDRUtil --probe=driver=hackrf

Using the SoapySDR backend (HackRF / PlutoSDR):

  The new --soapy <args> option selects a SoapySDR device; --gain <dB> sets the
  RX gain (omit for a sensible default / AGC). Samples are captured at an integer
  multiple of 1.92 Msps and decimated with an anti-aliasing filter, because
  HackRF cannot sample as low as 1.92 Msps.

  # Search a band with a HackRF
  CellSearch --soapy "driver=hackrf" --gain 40 --freq-start 791e6 --freq-end 821e6

  # Track a cell with a HackRF
  LTE-Tracker --soapy "driver=hackrf" --gain 40 -f 806e6

  # PlutoSDR
  CellSearch --soapy "driver=plutosdr" --freq-start 791e6 --freq-end 821e6

------
Install (so CellSearch / LTE-Tracker can be run from any directory):
------
Linux (installs into /usr/local/bin, which is already on your PATH):
  sudo make install

macOS (Apple Silicon): install into the Homebrew prefix, no sudo needed.
Configure with that prefix, then install:
  cmake .. -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/homebrew
  make -j4
  make install
  # Now just run, from anywhere:
  #   CellSearch --soapy "driver=hackrf" --freq-start 806e6 --freq-end 821e6
  #   LTE-Tracker --soapy "driver=plutosdr" -f 806e6
If /opt/homebrew/bin is not on your PATH, add it (Apple Silicon Homebrew):
  echo 'export PATH="/opt/homebrew/bin:$PATH"' >> ~/.zshrc && source ~/.zshrc

------
Quick usage instructions:
------

Search for LTE carriers within a common LTE frequency range used in the US:
  CellSearch --freq-start 715e6 --freq-end 768e6

Start tracking LTE cells on frequency 739 MHz:
  LTE-Tracker -f 739000000

